      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1387 Nether Liberton, under Adam Forrester, helped rebuild St Giles Cathedral alongside Provost Andrew Yichtson.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liberton%2C_Edinburgh",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Liberton hosts a prehistoric standing stone just over six feet tall, a silent witness to ancient visitors.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liberton%2C_Edinburgh",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The old North British Railway’s Loanhead and Roslin branch once crossed Liberton, linking it to Edinburgh’s growing suburbs.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.scottish-places.info/towns/townhistory2739.html",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Liberton’s name, from Old English ‘hlith’ and ‘bere‑tūn’, likely means ‘barley farm on a hillside’.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
